onalga food items were identified, including sponges, tube worms, sea pens, and sea hares. Substratum and anthropogenic debris such as plastic bags and nylon cord were commonly recovered in diet samples.","author_count":3,"author_ids":["A5013971914","A5087060644","A5111381876"],"author_institution_ids":["I2803094215"],"authors":[{"id":"A5087060644","name":"Jeffrey A. Seminoff"},{"id":"A5013971914","name":"Antonio Resendiz"},{"id":"A5111381876","name":"Wallace J. Nichols"}],"ca_any_author":true,"ca_led":false,"cited_by_count":150,"doi":"https://doi.org/10.1670/0022-1511(2002)036[0447:doepgt]2.0.co;2","domain_tags":[],"facet_tags":["matrix:food_and_drink","matrix:marine"],"institution_ids":["I138006243","I2803094215"],"is_oa":false,"journal":"Journal of Herpetology","last_updated":"2026-11-10T11:39:43.021295","license":"","needs_review":false,"oa_status":"closed","oa_url":"https://doi.org/10.1670/0022-1511(2002)036[0447:doepgt]2.0.co;2","openalex_topics":["T10753","T11656","T12841"],"plastic_related":true,"plastic_tier":"core","primary_topic":"T11656","pub_date":"2002-09-01","study_type":"article","title":"Diet of East Pacific Green Turtles (Chelonia mydas) in the Central Gulf of California, M\u00e9xico","type":"article","work_id":"W2084016254","year":2002}]}
